<title>USA: Quaker, Triarc rally on Snapple deal.</title>
<headline>Quaker, Triarc rally on Snapple deal.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quaker Oats Co stock gained in early New York Stock Exchange trade, the shares jumping two points to 39-1/2, then settling back to 38-3/4, as investors toasted Quaker's decision to sell its Snapple beverage unit to Triarc Cos Inc.</p>
<p>Triarc shares, meanwhile, were initially halted on the NYSE due to an order imbalance, then opened with a 2-1/4 gain to 18. The shares then settled back to 17-5/8.</p>
<p>&quot;Everyone knows it (Snapple) was a drag on their (Quaker's earnings). So the surprising news is not that they are selling, but that they found a buyer,&quot; said a trader.</p>
</text>
